00:37:04.470 --> 00:37:31.230
<v Aziz Ansari>Was that, like, what you were really thinking. Like, you know, we could have just-- so then, the next night, you send her the equivalent of your first contact, if you will. And you say, "It was cool meeting you last night. I'll be back in Cali in two weeks for winter break. We should hang out some time. Ha ha." It wasn't necessarily a Young Jeezy ha ha. It was just a ha ha.

00:37:31.230 --> 00:37:38.120
<v Jonathan Manjivar>So four guys, which one did this best? Aziz and Eric turn to the women in the audience.

00:37:38.120 --> 00:37:46.310
<v Aziz Ansari>Why don't we see which one do you guys like the most? Just the women in the audience. Clap if your favorite is this.

00:37:46.310 --> 00:37:54.900
<v Jonathan Manjivar>So the clear winner, the guy who wrote about Thanksgiving. "Hey there. How'd your Thanksgiving feast turn out? Here's a shot of the spread I put together."

00:37:54.900 --> 00:38:00.150
<v Eric Klinenberg>But could we find out from someone here what is so good about that text? If you voted for that text--

00:38:00.150 --> 00:38:01.730
<v Aziz Ansari>Yeah, raise your hand.

00:38:01.730 --> 00:38:12.340
<v Jonathan Manjivar>A woman in the audience, who's a little off mic, says it gets the conversation going. You asked a question. And he said something about his Thanksgiving, and it made you want to comment on it.

00:38:12.340 --> 00:38:13.920
<v Aziz Ansari>OK. Anybody else?

00:38:13.920 --> 00:38:17.950
<v Jonathan Manjivar>It was personal, another woman says. He remembered what you talked about.

00:38:17.950 --> 00:38:19.910
<v Aziz Ansari>Personal, remember what you talked about.

00:38:19.910 --> 00:38:26.550
<v Eric Klinenberg>You guys taking notes over there, by the way? Same time, we kind of need to know what didn't work out so well with the texts that nobody voted for.

00:38:26.550 --> 00:38:27.780
<v Aziz Ansari>What did you not like about--

00:38:27.780 --> 00:38:29.660
<v Eric Klinenberg>Oh, yeah, all the way in the back.

00:38:29.660 --> 00:38:39.430
<v Jonathan Manjivar>The woman in the back doesn't like the "what's up" guy who met someone at a wedding and texted her after she left. In fact, no one liked that text. It got zero claps.

00:38:39.430 --> 00:38:49.520
<v Jonathan Manjivar>The woman says, it sounded like he just wanted to have sex. He's saying, I don't live here. But I'm going to be back. Let's hang out. And I don't want to talk to you until then.

00:38:49.520 --> 00:38:51.910
<v Aziz Ansari>What do you mean? Why do you think he doesn't want to talk to her until then?

00:38:51.910 --> 00:38:54.300
<v Woman 1>Because he would have asked a question.

00:38:54.300 --> 00:38:58.530
<v Aziz Ansari>He would have asked a question. Does anyone else feel like that?

00:38:58.530 --> 00:39:00.490
